@namespace SpaceSails.Client.Pages
@implements IHandleEvent
@using SatchelPage = SpaceSails.Client.Pages.Map.SatchelPage
@*
    #251 · THE SATCHEL'S TITLE LINE, ON ITS OWN FILE.

    THE ONE LINE AT THE TOP THAT NAMES THE PAGE YOU ARE ON. Six answers to one question, because a
    page title here is the QUESTION the page answers ("why you are down here") and never the tab's own
    word said twice — and the bin's is the FIXTURE's name, or the bare verb once the bucket has walked
    off.

    Moved out of SatchelPanel.razor by PURE MOTION — the block between the two fences below is the block
    that was in the panel, character for character. Every member it reads is a [Parameter] with the SAME
    NAME (a field keeps its underscore, a method arrives as a delegate under its own name, a variable the
    panel's `@if` bound arrives under the name that binding gave it), which is what lets the markup move
    without a rewrite and lets the composition splice it straight back where it came from.

    IHandleEvent repeats SatchelPanel's own override, which repeats Map.Sim.cs's: the HUD's refresh
    belongs to OnTick's 200 ms throttle, and a child that did not repeat it would put an automatic render
    back on every event in here. The .razor.css beside this file carries no rules of its own, and its scope is the
    PAGE's own (b-4dqsdx4p75, pinned in SpaceSails.Client.csproj), so every rule that styled this markup
    goes on matching it.

    The `@{ }` around the fences is not decoration: the block came out of a Razor CODE block, and a code
    block is where its first statements are legal. It is outside the fences, so what the composition reads
    is exactly the lines that stood in the panel.
*@
@{
@* ── MARKUP BEGINS · verbatim from SatchelPanel.razor ────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
                <div class="view-object-title">
                    @(_satchelPage switch
                    {
                        SatchelPage.Notes => "📓 WHAT YOU WROTE DOWN",
                        // #741 v1 · Not the tab's own word twice over: a page title is the QUESTION the page
                        // answers, the way the compass's is ("why you are down here").
                        SatchelPage.Threads => "🧵 WHAT YOU WROTE DOWN TWICE",
                        SatchelPage.Spread => "🗂 THE PAPERS, OUT ON THE TABLE",
                        // #828 · The bucket is NAMED, and it is the one the boots are at — never "a bin".
                        // Away from one the title falls back to the verb, because a page whose fixture has
                        // walked off is a page about the verb and nothing else.
                        SatchelPage.Bin => BinWithinReach() is { } titleBin
                            ? SpaceSails.Core.RipAndBin.PickerTitle(titleBin.Tier)
                            : SpaceSails.Core.RipAndBin.Label,
                        // #727 · Not "your missions" — WHY YOU ARE DOWN HERE, which is the question the page
                        // answers and the one a captain three floors into a basement is actually asking.
                        SatchelPage.Missions => "🗺 WHY YOU ARE DOWN HERE",
                        _ => "🎒 WHAT YOU ARE CARRYING",
                    })
                </div>
@* ── MARKUP ENDS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@
}
